{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_multisinklogger", "label": "MultiSinkLogger", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Faechert jeden Record an mehrere Ziele gleichzeitig auf, jedes mit eigenem Mindest-Level. withLogSinks ist die Kurzform: das System verpackt die Liste, uebergibt den Sinks seinen Scheduler und flusht sie beim Terminieren."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_why_not_a_custom_logger", "label": "Warum nicht einen eigenen Logger schreiben", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Kann man \u2014 was eine handgeschriebene Implementierung nicht liefert, ist der leicht falsch gemachte Teil: der Record wird einmal gebaut statt einmal pro Ziel, ein kaputtes Ziel bleibt allein kaputt, die Zustellung ist begrenzt, und der Shutdown flusht innerhalb einer Frist."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_consolesink", "label": "ConsoleSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rendert text (byte-genau das, was ConsoleLogger schon immer schrieb, positionale Argumente unveraendert an console.*) und json (ein NDJSON-Objekt pro Zeile, bis hin zur Schluesselreihenfolge von JsonLogger)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_per_sink_min_level", "label": "Zwei Gates: System-Level und minLevel", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Das System-Level entscheidet, was ueberhaupt entsteht; das minLevel eines Sinks verengt nur weiter. Ein Sink, der debug verlangt, waehrend das System-Level info ist, bekommt nichts \u2014 genau diese Reihenfolge haelt einen unterdrueckten Log-Aufruf so billig wie einen Vergleich."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_transform_hook", "label": "transform-Hook", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Laeuft einmal vor dem Auffaechern, damit jedes Ziel denselben redigierten Record sieht und es keine Frage gibt, welches den Rohwert bekam. Er laeuft auf dem Stack des Aufrufers, muss also billig und total sein; wirft er, wird gemeldet und der Record unveraendert behalten, weil den Log-Strom still zu loeschen der schlimmere Fehlerfall ist."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_batchingsink", "label": "BatchingSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Basisklasse jedes Sinks, der auf einen Dateideskriptor oder Netzwerk-Endpunkt schreibt, damit max-batch-size, flush-interval, queue-capacity, overflow, max-retries und die Backoff-Grenzen ueberall dasselbe bedeuten. Gebuendelt wird im Intervall und sofort bei vollem Batch, weil ein Burst sonst ein ganzes Intervall Latenz zahlte."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_bounded_queue_overflow", "label": "Die Queue ist begrenzt", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ist sie voll, faellt ein Record \u2014 standardmaessig der neueste, mit drop-head der aelteste \u2014, die Zahl steht auf droppedCount und wird hoechstens einmal pro Minute gemeldet. Ein unbegrenzter Puffer rettet die Records nicht; er verwandelt \"einige Logs gingen verloren\" in \"der Prozess ist gestorben\"."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_sinkdeliveryerror_retry_policy", "label": "SinkDeliveryError trennt wiederholenswert von nicht", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein wiederholbarer Fehler wird exponentiell mit Jitter zurueckgestellt und respektiert eine vom Server vorgegebene Wartezeit; ein nicht wiederholbarer (401 wegen falschem API-Key) wird sofort verworfen, weil fuenf Retries nur den Moment verzoegern, in dem es jemand merkt. Ein Fehler, der kein SinkDeliveryError ist, gilt als wiederholbar \u2014 so sieht ein Socket-Reset aus."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_shutdown_flush", "label": "Flush beim Shutdown", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "terminate() flusht und schliesst die Sinks vor whenTerminated(), begrenzt durch close-timeout; der Flush laeuft nach dem postStop jedes Actors, eine Abschiedsnachricht ist also noch im Batch. Ein haengendes Ziel kann den Prozess nicht festhalten, und Records nach dem Schliessen fallen auf eine Konsolenzeile zurueck. Beim Schliessen wird ohne Retries geleert, weil der Schliessende schon eine Frist haelt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_logsink_contract", "label": "Der LogSink-Vertrag", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "name, minLevel und write reichen. Drei Regeln machen einen Sink sicher genug: write wirft nie, write blockiert nie, und ein Sink loggt nie ueber den Framework-Logger \u2014 er ist der Framework-Logger, einen Fehler so zu melden fuettert ihn zurueck in das, was fehlgeschlagen ist. Dafuer gibt es SinkReporter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_logger_configuration_precedence", "label": "Code und Konfiguration werden nicht gemischt", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "withLogger ersetzt alles, withLogSinks ersetzt den kompletten sinks-Block statt ihn zu ergaenzen, dann die aktivierten HOCON-Bloecke, zuletzt der einzelne ConsoleLogger. Ein Ziel wird an der einen oder anderen Stelle beschrieben \u2014 Optionen werden in dem Konstruktor validiert, dem sie gehoeren, was nur geht, wenn dieser alle sieht."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_multisinklogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_per_sink_min_level", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_multisinklogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_transform_hook", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_multisinklogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_shutdown_flush", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_multisinklogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_logger_configuration_precedence", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_multisinklogger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_logsink_contract", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_why_not_a_custom_logger", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_multisinklogger", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_consolesink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_logsink_contract", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_consolesink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_per_sink_min_level", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_batchingsink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_logsink_contract", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_bounded_queue_overflow", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_batchingsink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_sinkdeliveryerror_retry_policy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_batchingsink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_shutdown_flush", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_batchingsink", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_logsink_contract", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_batchingsink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_bounded_queue_overflow", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_overview_outbound_buffer", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_sinkdeliveryerror_retry_policy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_io_overview_reconnect_with_backoff", "relation": "semantically_similar_to", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}], "hyperedges": [{"id": "batching_log_sink_delivery_pipeline", "label": "Log-Sinks auf der gemeinsamen BatchingSink-Zustellung", "nodes": ["docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_multi_sink_batchingsink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_file_sink_filesink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_integrations_otlphttpsink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_integrations_gelfsink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_integrations_lokisink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_integrations_seqsink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_integrations_splunksink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_integrations_syslogsink", "docs_src_content_docs_de_observability_logging_integrations_parseablesink"], "relation": "implement", "confidence": "INFERRED", "confidence_score": 0.85, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/observability/logging/multi-sink.mdx"}]}